%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against tests/ on disk + D36 + D75 + B7
flowchart TB
    U["<b>UNIT</b> - tests/unit/, 18 files<br/>state machine, orchestrator, domain pack, prompt pack,<br/>identity resolver, IVR walk, context + brief, matching,<br/>presence + assignment, capture, queue hours, diagrams"]:::unit
    C["<b>CONTRACT SUITES</b> - tests/contracts/, 5 files<br/>every adapter for a port must pass the SAME suite, and the<br/>store suite runs three times: <b>in-memory / SQLite / Postgres</b>.<br/>This is what makes a hackathon-day swap safe: the new<br/>adapter either passes or it does not ship. (D75)"]:::contract
    I["<b>INTEGRATION</b> - tests/integration/<br/>boots a real app over real HTTP, <b>throws it away</b>,<br/>boots a second on the same storage and asks what it knows.<br/>The only shape that can prove a restart."]:::integ
    S["<b>SCENARIOS</b> - 3 scripted calls, end to end<br/>pattheera_ipd - roadside_motor_claim - anonymous_declined<br/>byte-identical on replay, with expect: blocks checked"]:::scen

    U --> C --> I --> S
    S --> TOT["<b>496 tests, about 100 seconds</b><br/>454 pass + 42 skip with no container;<br/>493 pass + 3 skip with Postgres up — the three<br/>are FK cases a dict cannot have"]:::tot

    DET["<b>why replays are byte-identical</b><br/>ManualClock + DeterministicIds are INJECTED (D35).<br/>Nothing calls datetime.now() or makes a random id<br/>on its own, so the same scenario produces the same<br/>output every time — which is what makes golden<br/>comparison possible at all."]:::note

    B7["<b>the gap none of these layers closes by itself (B7).</b><br/>Every test drove the system through endpoints, and endpoints<br/>tick the dispatcher on the way through — so the suite proved<br/>the ticking WORKED without proving anything CAUSED it. Three<br/>services fired only because time passed, and all three were<br/>driven by nothing. Anything time-driven needs a test in which<br/><b>only time passes</b>."]:::warn

    FRESH["<b>three freshness checks, same argument.</b> Generated diagrams,<br/>the voice-prompt manifest, and the keypad page's embedded menu<br/>data are each regenerated into a temp copy and compared. A<br/>committed artefact that silently falls behind is worse than a<br/>missing one, because it is convincing."]:::note

    HAND["<b>grep -rn '# P1:' scripts/</b><br/>lists every lifecycle step the runner still does by hand.<br/>P3 took the IVR ones over; what is left is the media<br/>gateway, the named agent, and the agent-side rating.<br/>The handover list is executable, not prose. (D36)"]:::note

